(SafeFlow PDF Export Review) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Generated as a review artifact for the PDF export hardening work.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What Changed) Tj
T*
(- The PDF/print export no longer interpolates RAMS data into an HTML string.) Tj
T*
(- The export now opens a print window and constructs the document using DOM nodes and textContent.) Tj
T*
(- Risk labels are normalised to known CSS classes before being applied.) Tj
T*
(- Generated text, user-entered text, and AI-returned content are treated as text, not executable markup.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why It Matters) Tj
T*
(- The previous implementation used document.write with generated RAMS fields embedded directly in HTML.) Tj
T*
(- HTML-like generated values could alter the exported document structure.) Tj
T*
(- The new path assigns RAMS content through text nodes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Verification) Tj
T*
(- npm run build passes.) Tj
T*
(- OpenAI calls now use shared error handling through lib/openaiClient.js.) Tj
T*
(- The job description field is now a larger textarea labelled Tell us about the job.) Tj
T*
(- Supabase and OpenAI environment variables are present locally.) Tj
ET
